instructorProvidedContent.typicalTopicsAndOrSchedule:
Topics/Techniques/Technologies may include:
The Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)
Waterfall vs Agile development;
Scrum and Extreme Programming (XP);
Requirements gathering;
Version control/planning/management using Git, GitLab and other tools;
Docker;
DevOps and Continuous Integration/Deployment;
Client-server and MVC architecture;
Design Patterns;
Code documentation (e.g. javadoc);
Unit testing and System testing (e.g. jUnit, Mockito);
Database integration and Object Relational Mapping (e.g. JDBC, SqlAlchemy, Hibernate);
Comment-first and test-first development;
Pair programming;
Authentication and/or Security;
UIX & HCI;
Etc.
Typical weekly schedule might be:
0: Introduction to SWE concepts and the SDLC
1: Agile/Scrum ; Docker ; Requirements ; Estimation ; GitLab with Git
2: SQL/MySQL ; REST / MVC ; JDBC / ORM ; GitLab project management ; (Project: Team Assignments and Project Kickoffs )
3: Docker ; REST/Gradle; JUnit / TD ; (Project: Weekly Scrum; Architecture Planning)
4: Postman / Mockito ; (Project: Sprint 0 Review; Sprint 1 Planning)
5: GitLab CI/CD ; Software Design Principles; (Project: Weekly Scrum; Architecture Planning)
6: Software Design Principles; Design Patterns; (Project: Sprint 1 Review; Sprint 2 Planning)
7: MIDTERM ; Software Design Principles; Design Patterns; (Project: Code Reviews; Weekly Scrum; Architecture Planning)
8: Software Design Principles; (Project: Weekly Scrum; Code Reviews)
9: Software Design Principles; Agile/Scrum ; (Project: Sprint 2 Review; Sprint 3 Planning)
10: PRACTICAL EXAMS; Extreme Programming; Software Design Principles; (Weekly Scrum; Code Reviews)
11: PRACTICAL EXAMS; Software Design Principles; (Project: Weekly Scrum; Architecture Planning)
12: (Project: Weekly Scrum)
13: Software Engineering Ethics; (Project: Sprint 3 Review; Plan Final Demo)
14: Software Engineering Recap; Software Engineering Disasters; (Project: Final Demos)
15: FINAL EXAM

